MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The duct tape felt useful because it can secure loose materials and support general workshop repairs alongside my fasteners and hooks.",
    "The tape fit my interest in practical supplies with several everyday uses, without requiring a specific new project."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "Test leads, heat-shrink supplies, wire connectors and a bench power supply assume an electrical project; buying nuts, bolts and magnetic hooks does not mean I need wiring equipment.",
    "The medical tests, disposable gloves and cleaning brushes do not help with the mounting, fastening and organization tasks suggested by my recent purchases. A thousand gloves also feels excessive without an immediate need."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The recommendations seemed to treat workshop supplies as interchangeable, even though electrical testing serves a different purpose from fastening and hanging things.",
    "My screw kit's mention of electronics seemed to receive too much weight compared with my repeated purchases of hooks and other fastening supplies."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My recent purchases repeatedly involve attaching, securing or hanging things; that shared purpose matters more to me than whether something belongs in a workshop.",
    "I rarely choose something just because it might be useful someday. Specialized equipment needs to match a task I actually have, while versatile repair supplies are easier to justify."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations partly recognized my interest in practical workshop supplies but stretched it into electrical, medical and cleaning needs that my recent purchases do not support."
}
